# The image needs the demo batch (one-click run), the training batch (the review screen
# shows narrations and amounts as evidence), and the seeded run.
#
# data/test/ IS shipped, and the reason it is no longer excluded is worth recording. While
# the seal was intact this file kept the held-out set out of the image so that the seal
# meant something in every artifact, not only in the repository. The seal was broken once,
# at Phase 7, and the set has been scored and reported -- so excluding it now would buy no
# protection and would cost the demo its evidence: the live URL would show a run at an
# operating point the project pre-committed against.
#
# data/test/.unsealed travels with it. That file carries the sha256 map forward from
# .sealed, so a reviewer who pulls the image can verify the served numbers were computed
# from the bytes that were sealed. tests/test_seal.py enforces the same map in the repo,
# and tests/test_deployment.py enforces that the marker is shipped.
